      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Architecture of the proposed ERBA. It augments a sequence-only PLM with multimodal conditioning on substrate chemistry and pocket geometry. MRCA injects substrate fingerprints into enzyme embeddings to capture recognition specificity, and G-MoE integrates local 3D pocket structure to model conformational adaptation. Update and query paths couple both modules to the backbone, while ESDA aligns representations with the prior PLM, enabling accurate prediction of enzyme kinetic parameters.",
