    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-e65aefda57f7",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. The pipeline of the proposed method. Our framework consists of two key components: (1) Dynamic Perception for Global Pose, which addresses the inherent ambiguity of symmetric local structures by estimating a globally consistent reference rotation Rg through Bingham distribution modeling, generating adaptive anchor points that provide additional global cues; (2) 4D Robust Modeling for Local Representation, where constructs LRFs {Lj}k j=1 and a learnable steerable transform (ST ) lifts the point cloud into 4D space, enabling fine-grained geometric encoding and enhancing the robustness of local representations against point-pair ambiguity. Finally, a Rotation- Invariant Convolution module embeds and aggregates the resulting Ga4DPF features, producing discriminative representations suitable for downstream tasks such as shape classification and part segmentation.",
