      "id": "cvpr26-ce76673e1ffa",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. An illustration of using SCM to model the data generation process for vision data and our uncertainty-augmented Bayesian framework, CGU-BAYES. For the SCM causal graph, black edges denote known relationships, green edges indicate possible acyclic edges, and red edges highlight domain-dependent relations influenced by U. In CGU-BAYES, multiple CMB sets are selected across sampled Gs, robust predictors are constructed, and their uncertainties are used as weights to aggregate predictions for the final output.",
