      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3. Overview of Upsample Anything. Given a high-resolution image Ihr, we downsample it to Ilr and optimize GSJBU to recon- struct Ihr, learning per-pixel anisotropic kernels {σx, σy, θ, σr} via test-time optimization (TTO). The learned kernels are then applied to foundation features Flr for rendering the high-resolution features Fhr, achieving pixel-wise anisotropic joint bilateral upsampling.",
