  {
    "id": "cvpr26-de9ac3627ea8",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-de9ac3627ea8",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Overview of different hypernetwork approaches for parameter prediction. (a) Graph Hypernetwork (GHN) encodes model architecture as a graph and predicts parameters through a hypernetwork, updated via task loss. (b) Following the same framework as (a) with identical inputs and loss computation, Task-Aware Learngene (TAL) pretrains the hypernetwork on large datasets using soft labels from a pre-trained model, then fine-tunes on multiple tasks to enable task-specific parameter prediction. (c) Following the same framework as (a) with identical inputs and loss computation, Parameter InheritTance Hypernetwork (PITH) introduces a dual-pathway decoder: a projection pathway that generates projection matrices to inherit pre-trained parameters Wp (used as fixed input without updates) into target parameters Wproj, and an original pathway for residual prediction Wpred, combined to produce final target model weights.",
      "page": 3,
      "captionRect": [
        58.5,
        219.0561065673828,
        553.4992065429688,
        294.059814453125
      ],
