      "id": "cvpr26-baddce209f69",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Our SAMTok architecture. SAMTok has a encoder fenc, a vector quantizer with codebook C, and a decoder fdec. Both fenc and fdec are instantiated with a SAM model, which includes an image backbone fimg, a prompt encoder fprm, and a mask decoder fmsk. Given an input image I and a region M (e.g., the area out- lined in purple), the SAMTok encoder fenc first encodes the 2D mask into a mask embedding z, then performs two-stage quantiza- tion to obtain a discrete mask embeddings [e1, e2]. The SAMTok decoder fdec reconstructs the 2D mask ˆ M from the original image and the region’s discrete mask embeddings.",
