      "id": "cvpr26-60c50560d3b4",
      "figure": "Figure 6",
      "caption": "Figure 6. The overall structure of our Detect-Mitigate framework. It consists of three components. First, Logit-Lens Consistency Check (LLCC) detects hallucinated object tokens in the response. Then, High-Attention Regions Masking (HARM) categorizes them into two different types of hallucination while generating an intermediate output. If type 2 hallucination is detected, the output is further processed by Visual Evidence Enhanced Decoding (VEED) to produce the final result.",
