    "id": "cvpr26-ab3bb2a310d7",
    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3 : Overview of the SARMAE pretraining framework. The framework consists of two branches: (i) a SAR branch following the MAE architecture with Speckle-Aware Representation Enhancement (SARE) to handle inherent speckle noise, and (ii) an optical branch using a frozen DINOv3 encoder. For paired SAR-optical data, Semantic Anchor Representation Constraint (SARC) aligns SAR features with semantic-rich optical representations. Unpaired SAR images are processed solely through the SAR branch.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2512.16635v2/images/model.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S3.F3",
      "panelIndex": 0,
