      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. The overall architecture of our proposed GuideFlow. GuideFlow begins by encoding multi-view images into feature maps, followed by scene representation learning through the perception module. The encoded sample xt is then fused with scene representation and subjected to dynamic condition guidance for vt prediction. The vt is subsequently rectified by our proposed strategy {CVF, CF and RFE} ((Sec. 4.3)), ultimately sampling the driving trajectory. “R” denotes “Reward”.",
