      "id": "cvpr26-50124351f6cc",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. The pipeline of JUMP-Hand. (a) Joint-wise uncertainty modeling: each view independently predicts 2D joint locations and uncertainties (µn, σn) supervised by NLL loss. H and V represents heatmap head and variance head respectively. (b) Uncertainty is converted to explicit joint-wise gating signal to guide coarse-to-fine reconstruction. (c) Coarse stage: uncertainty-guided DLT (UG- DLT) performs weighted triangulation to obtain robust 3D initialization. (d) Refinement stage: refined iterative regression through query modeling. Uncertainty-gated cross attention (UGCA) is the core to fuse each view’s features through gating mechanism.",
      "page": 4,
      "captionRect": [
        58.5,
        243.85598754882812,
        553.5010986328125,
