    "id": "cvpr26-6af405e858e2",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-6af405e858e2",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. SAGE Workflow. Our system accepts four inputs (shown at the top): sampled video frames (F), metadata about the video (M), available tool definitions (T), and the user query (Q). Given these inputs, SAGE operates in two stages based on the role of SAGE-MM. In Stage-1, SAGE-MM is responsible for providing information about the video’s context (C) along with either a final answer prediction or a tool call to be executed before the next step. At every subsequent step in Stage-2, SAGE-MM uses the video context (C) and the tool call results from previous steps to decide either to predict the final answer or call another tool in an iterative reasoning process.",
      "page": 3,
      "captionRect": [
        58.5,
