  {
    "id": "cvpr26-b976c4e327fd",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-b976c4e327fd",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of TADSR. We train a Student Model Gθ to perform one-step Real-ISR, which consists of a Time-Aware VAE Encoder Eθ and a UNet Fθ. We randomly sample a timestep ts and map it to tv. The ts and the LQ image are fed into the encoder Eθ to obtain the LQ latent. Then, ts and the LQ latent are fed into the UNet Fθ to produce the reconstructed latent feature ˆz0. After adding noise to ˆz0 corresponding to tv, we feed it and tv into the teacher model and the LoRA model to compute the TAVSD loss (orange flow). The reconstruction loss (blue flow) in pixel space and TAVSD loss is then used to jointly update the student model Gθ. For the LoRA Model, we employ the diffusion loss (green flow) for training.",
      "page": 3,
      "captionRect": [
        58.5,
        271.0554504394531,
        553.5033569335938,
        335.0233154296875
      ],
