  {
    "id": "cvpr26-e344901a9b30",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-e344901a9b30",
      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3. The overview structure of UniChange is shown in (a). UniChange generates text outputs based on text instructions and dual- temporal remote sensing images. The text outputs incorporate a series of special tokens ([T1], [T2], and [CHANGE]). Concurrently, the dual-temporal remote sensing images undergo feature extraction via the Vision Backbone. These features, alongside the embeddings corresponding to the special tokens, are fed into the Token Driven Decoder. Ultimately, UniChange generates the masks corresponding to the text instructions. The overall structure of the Token Driven Decoder is shown in (b). It receives dual-temporal remote sensing image features and special token embeddings, generating corresponding masks.",
      "page": 4,
      "captionRect": [
        58.5,
        290.7389831542969,
        553.4991455078125,
        354.49932861328125
      ],
      "score": -6,
