  {
    "id": "cvpr26-d820e138f804",
    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3 : An overview of the TeFlow , a multi-frame feedforward scene flow estimation pipeline, shown in the top row.\nOur self-supervised pipeline tackles the main challenge of deriving reliable supervision f ¯ \\bar{\\textbf{f}} from dense multi-frame inputs.\nFor each dynamic cluster 𝒞 j \\mathcal{C}_{j} , we constructs a motion candidate pool (internal f ^ 𝒞 j \\hat{\\textbf{f}}_{\\mathcal{C}_{j}} and external 𝐟 𝒞 j , k \\mathbf{f}_{\\mathcal{C}_{j},k} ). Candidates are processed via a weighted consensus voting scheme using directional consistency 𝐌 \\mathbf{M} and magnitude-based reliability 𝐰 \\mathbf{w} to find a consensus winner ( Equation 7 ). The final supervision 𝐟 ¯ 𝒞 j \\bar{\\mathbf{f}}_{\\mathcal{C}_{j}} is a weighted average of the winner and agreeing candidates, which filters inconsistent outliers (e.g., f ^ 𝒞 j , 1 \\hat{\\textbf{f}}_{\\mathcal{C}_{j},1} ) for stable training.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2602.19053v2/TeFlow-method-fig-v2-cvpr.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S3.F3",
      "panelIndex": 0,
      "panelCount": 1,
