    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-51e90f31b99e",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Chorus Overview. (a) Multi-Teacher Pretraining. We train a feed-forward 3DGS scene encoder to distill complementary signals–language-aligned (SigLIP), generalist (DINO), and object-aware (PE)–from 2D teachers. This knowledge is transferred into a shared embedding space via lightweight per-teacher projectors and losses. To accelerate out-of-domain adaptation, we support finetuning the encoder with online rendering-based supervision. (b) Task-Specific Transfer. Pretrained Chorus encoder enables diverse downstream tasks, including semantic and instance segmentation, open-vocabulary query, and 3D visual question answering (VQA).",
      "page": 3,
      "captionRect": [
        58.5,
